The chances of your getting an artifact are 1/(10 + 2 � Number of
existing artifacts � Number of gifts granted by your god).

You now have 4 to 6 gifts.  That gives the odds of a gift as 1/(10 +
2*4*4) = 1-in-42 to 1/(10 + 2*6*6) = 1-in-82.

Generally the chances of a gift is a factor of ten lower than you want
to expect.  That's mostly because the chances start so low it's hard to
comprehend how low they go so fast.  If you've sacrificed hundred of
times, now you need to sacrifice thousands of times. It's how the
numbers work out.

But you don't actually want to sacrifice all that much any more.  If you
are interested in getting crowned every sacrifice intended to get
another artifact gift is a waste of time.

> Praying just tells me my deity is enormously pleased (as he very well
> /should/ be) but I don't get crowned.

This suggests that your luck is not maxed out at +13.  The higher your
luck the more benefits you get at each prayer.  They include golden glow
for increased max hit points, blue aura for remove curse and unrust your
wielded weapon, spell books, points of protection.  If you have not been
getting those it is time to max out your luck.

Here's your process if you chose to ignore the fact that both Frost
Brand and Fire Brand beat Vorpal Blade:

Keep sacrificing until you are reconciled.  Then keep sacrificing until
you stop seeing clovers.  That means your luck is maxed out.  This is
the starting point of your loop.

Pray hoping to get crowned. After each prayer sacrifice again until
reconciled and pray again immediately.  Keep looping through these two
steps.

Once your luck is maxed out it won't take more than a few dozen cycles
to get crowned.  It will happen much faster if you don't actually intend
to get crowned.  Somehow the RNG reads are minds and does that to us.


